@@ -16,3 +16,15 @@ All pytest commands use `. .venv/bin/activate && python -m pytest`.
 12. `backend/tests/test_vc_recovery.py -q -k test_unknown_request_lifetime_disables_auto_clear`: RED audited human path unavailable (1 failed, 4 negatives passed); GREEN both files 32 cases. No deployment lifetime configured: auto-clear disabled even with caller reference. Human exception requires trusted policy, reason, risk acknowledgement, exact termination and >=3 stable post-termination observations; only verified-lifetime span is waived and auditable.
 13. `backend/tests/test_vc_coordination.py -q -k "test_crashes_between_evidence_cas_consumption_patch_and_release_remain_safe or test_checkpoint" --tb=short`: RED missing stage validation port/checkpoint (21 cases); GREEN `backend/tests/test_vc_coordination.py backend/tests/test_vc_recovery.py -q --tb=short` 53 cases. Eighteen boundary cases cover evidence, CAS, consumption, intent, receipt, release; monotonic checkpoints never replay. In-flight finish quarantines even matching GET. StageEvidence has no send-response field, so injected trusted digest verifier must prove synchronous completion; absent verifier fails closed. No M04 implementation import.
 14. `backend/tests/test_vc_coordination.py -q -k test_observer_cannot_regress_or_approve_heads --tb=short`: RED missing observation lease; GREEN both files 54 cases. Observer leases serialize with managed attempts, committed version attempt/generation/parent must match, observed only, delayed holder rejected. advance_heads finalizes an observer lease; approved/deployed require injected policy and verified deployment evidence.
+15. `backend/tests/test_vc_coordination.py -q -k test_conflict_facts_carry_the_rejected_requests_own_identity` (BLOCK-7): RED loser's conflict fact reported `actor.subject_id == 'coordination'`/winner identity and keys collided on `{op}:{attempt}:{row_version}:{status}`; GREEN both unit files 55 cases. `_fact` now takes an explicit `AttemptSubject`; CAS-loser attributes to the executor that tried (`attempt_id=None`); `event_key` = `{operation_id}:{attempt}:{kind}:{status}` (fact_kind in, row_version out) so kinds no longer collide and the key is stable across unrelated CAS.
+16. `backend/tests/test_vc_coordination.py -q -k test_consumption_and_termination_columns_are_truthful` + `backend/tests/test_vc_recovery.py -q -k "persists_validated_termination or crash_between_audit or invalid_termination"` (BLOCK-10): RED post-admit column read False despite durable+flushed consumption; checkpoint flipped it True for approval-less claims; termination_evidence never written on any recover path. GREEN both unit files 59 cases. `_publish_consumption(claim, row)` now records `approval_consumption_published=True` only when an approval is actually bound and a durable consumption fact was verified; checkpoint no longer sets it unconditionally. recover persists validated `termination_evidence` via CAS immediately after `_validate_termination` and before any fact append, so a crash between audit append and release leaves durable proof; `_release` still clears it. `_cas` read-back now compares JSON columns by canonical wire form so a stored dict equals its frozen/tuple read-back. Amended `test_admission_atomically_binds_...`: the admission binding is still exactly one `state=ADMITTED` CAS; the new consumption-column CAS binds no admission fields.
+17. `backend/tests/test_vc_coordination.py -q -k "definite_presend_rejection or drift_conflict"` (BLOCK-1): RED all five definite pre-send rejection causes left the row RESERVED+unresolved (holder/attempt/approval retained), so `observe_exclusively`/fresh `reserve` raised `Binding busy` and expiry escalated to QUARANTINED. GREEN both unit files 65 cases. Added `_presend`, `_history_raw`, and `_reject` (publish terminal conflict fact, read-back-verify, then `_release` — same ordering as finish; if the fact cannot be proven durable the row stays unresolved). `_history` re-expressed as `_history_raw` + digest predicate calling `_reject`. All six admit pre-send rejection sites plus the idempotency-digest path now call `_reject`, so a definite 409 frees the binding instead of bricking it; drift round-trips through observe_exclusively → advance_heads → reserve/admit.
+18. `backend/tests/test_vc_coordination.py -q -k "terminal_non_success or confirmed_and_noop or mixed_history_prefers"` (BLOCK-8): RED a FAILED/CONFLICTED receipt was returned via ExistingReceipt as a "completion", and a mixed FAILED+CONFIRMED history raised 'Ambiguous completed receipts'. GREEN both unit files 69 cases. reserve now partitions the receipt scan: only CONFIRMED/NOOP receipts short-circuit to ExistingReceipt; a terminal non-success receipt calls BLOCK-1's `_reject` (409 conflict, binding intact, points to a new governed request); ambiguity is checked over completed receipts only, so a CONFIRMED wins over a stale FAILED.
+19. `backend/tests/test_vc_recovery.py -q -k "reclaim or expired_observation or expired_admitted"` (BLOCK-2): RED an expired OBSERVING lease quarantined the binding (silently, no fact) across reserve/observe_exclusively/advance_heads. GREEN both unit files 75 cases. `_expire` now reclaims an expired OBSERVING row to IDLE via `_reclaim_observer` (generation+1, heads/observed_sequence preserved) instead of quarantining; a row mislabelled OBSERVING while carrying an approval/stage/admitted_at fails closed with AuthorityUnavailable and is left unchanged. Negative control: an expired ADMITTED lease still quarantines and still appends its QUARANTINED fact.
+20. `backend/tests/test_vc_coordination.py -q -k "finish_releases_only or finish_possible_send"` (BLOCK-6): RED confirmed-no-postimage / noop-no-postimage / compensation-attempted results stranded the row ADMITTED+unresolved (then quarantined on expiry). GREEN both unit files 81 cases. finish reordered: caller-identity mismatch (operation_id/preimage) is a 409 that touches no state; the in-flight/unresolved/applied_* possible-send guard still quarantines first (C5.7); a non-terminal status or a CONFIRMED/NOOP-without-postimage on a PROVEN pre-send row (`_presend`) routes through `_reject(status=FAILED)` to release the binding, otherwise raises leaving it unresolved. Negative controls preserved: caller error on a possible-send row quarantines; `verify_flush` failure keeps a valid CONFIRMED result unresolved (C5.8).
+21. `backend/tests/test_vc_coordination.py -q -k "stage_machine_is_scoped or replay_skip_and_attempt"` (BLOCK-12): RED the six-stage global PatchStage index arithmetic forced every operation through all stages (a config-only op could illegally advance into DESCRIPTION_PENDING; a description-only op could not checkpoint at all), and the checkpoint CAS fenced on mutation_stage alone, not the attempt. GREEN both unit files 85 cases. admit records the planned stage sequence in the checkpoint via `_planned_stages(authorization)` (getattr default = full march, NB-5); checkpoint scopes advance/replay/skip to that planned list and rejects stages not in it; recorded_at/stale-stage bounds are a separate distinguishable raise (NB-4); the CAS now fences `r.attempt_id == claim.attempt_id AND r.mutation_stage == row.mutation_stage`. `approval_consumption_published=True` stays removed (BLOCK-10). Existing normal-sequence test still green under the default plan.
+22. `backend/tests/test_vc_recovery.py -q -k "closes_the_operation or recovery_publication_failure"` (BLOCK-5): RED recover appended only a RECOVERY fact and released, leaving the key with no RECEIPT so the same idempotency_key could be reserved+admitted again (M04 re-issues the PATCH for an unknown-outcome attempt). GREEN both unit files 88 cases. recover now appends both a RECOVERY audit and a terminal RECEIPT (both CONFLICTED, post_version_id None) via BLOCK-7's fact_kind-bearing distinct keys, read-back-verifies BOTH via `_history_raw`, and only then releases; a read-back failure keeps the row QUARANTINED. NOTE deviation from BLOCK-5(d) assertion 4: after BLOCK-8 a CONFLICTED receipt is a conflict, not a completion, so the second same-key reserve raises CoordinationError via `_reject` (not ExistingReceipt) — the safety property (no Reservation, no AdmissionClaim, binding intact) holds and is asserted; a different idempotency_key still admits.
+23. `backend/tests/test_vc_recovery.py -q -k classification_is_derived` (BLOCK-11): RED recover accepted any non-blank `checkpoint_classification` (the diff's 'observed-preimage' passed for every stage) and recorded the caller's string as durable audit truth. GREEN both unit files 92 cases. Added `_classification(row)` deriving the value from durable state (recorded resume_classification; else in-flight->read-only-possible-send; else never-admitted/presend by admitted_at). recover now requires the caller value to equal the derived one and `replace`s evidence with the derived string before appending, so the RECOVERY/RECEIPT facts carry authoritative classification. Amended `recovery_evidence` helper to default classification='read-only-presend' (the admit+quarantine path's derived value) — justified by C5.9 'classify against checkpoint'.
+24. `backend/tests/test_vc_coordination.py -q -k "reservation_fence_cannot_advance or empty_head_update or admission_claim_can_advance"` (BLOCK-3): RED a bare RESERVED Reservation fence could set observed/approved/deployed heads (policy callback was the only 'gate' and it never fired for a never-admitted attempt), and an all-None update silently consumed an observer lease. GREEN both unit files 97 cases. advance_heads now rejects an empty update, and for any non-observer write requires `isinstance(fence, AdmissionClaim)` then `assert_owner` (re-verifies ADMITTED + request/approval/preimage vs the durable row) BEFORE the authorize_heads policy callback, so a reservation can no longer write governed heads. Positive control: an admitted authorized claim still advances all three heads; a tampered claim request_digest is rejected.
+25. `backend/tests/test_vc_coordination.py -q -k "require_committed_versions or positive_control_and_earlier"` (BLOCK-9): RED approved/deployed heads flowed straight into the CAS with no ledger resolution, so an unknown id, a foreign-binding version, an old-revision version, or an uncommitted id all became this binding's approved/deployed head (authorize_heads, a boolean policy oracle, was the only 'gate'). GREEN both unit files 106 cases. Added `_committed_head(row, version_id, name)` resolving via ledger.get_version, requiring version.context.binding == row.binding and verify_committed(ref); advance_heads calls it for approved/deployed BEFORE authorize_heads (evidence before policy). Deliberate asymmetry with observed: no attempt_id/generation equality on approved/deployed, so a version captured under an earlier attempt is a valid approved head (positive control).
+26. `backend/tests/test_vc_coordination.py -q -k cannot_regress` (BLOCK-4): RED approved/deployed heads were written with `x or row.heads.x` and no lineage guard, so approved could regress to an ancestor, deployed could lead approved, and an off-lineage id was accepted. GREEN both unit files 107 cases. Added `_advances(binding, current, candidate)` walking committed parent lineage via ledger.get_version with a cycle guard (fails closed on a corrupted cycle). advance_heads enforces per-head monotonicity along committed lineage and the C5.8 cross-head rule (deployed must not lead approved), and the three head assignments use explicit `is None` tests (NB-3). Existing observer/admit head test still green.
